WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.300
Missing information is a design choice not something
we should leave accidental

00:00:06.035 --> 00:00:11.564
NULL represents unknown missing or not-applicable
information It is not the

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:17.402
same as zero an empty string or false For each
column ask

00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:22.963
whether missingness makes sense A patient medical
record number may be

00:00:22.976 --> 00:00:28.742
required so it should not be nullable Email may be
optional An

00:00:28.768 --> 00:00:34.123
appointment start time is required for a scheduled
appointment A cancellation time

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.229
only makes sense when an appointment is cancelled so
it may be

00:00:37.255 --> 00:00:43.279
nullable A data dictionary documents these decisions
It

00:00:43.306 --> 00:00:48.463
should describe the column meaning type nullability
units keys and important business

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:54.405
rules This documentation helps future analysts
interpret the database

00:00:54.418 --> 00:00:55.010
correctly
